{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1148214-chronicler-s-guide-and-other-1ed-books","id":1148214,"title":"Chronicler's Guide and other 1ed books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-08T20:43:52-07:00","id":1148214,"title":"Chronicler's Guide and other 1ed books","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Since the advent of the second edition, moast of the crunch (and some of the fluff) of the setting has been reworked, are there any plans to make second-edition-compliant versions of old books? Or a guide to update them?<br /> <br /> Specifically, I am looking for the ideas in the Chronicler's Guide ( I just love the concept of Soul Mods, getting a legacy attainment for practical reasons and getting drawbacks for doing so!) and how to update them to second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T02:53:20-07:00","id":1148260,"title":"","content":"There's not really any plans to directly update anything from first edition outside the core, no. There's still a lot of unexplored territory in Mage and <i>most</i> of the fluff from 1e is still fine, so, given the limited number of people, time, and money, the investment's going into new stuff.<br /> <br /> As far as updating goes, try it out for yourself and see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T16:31:11-07:00","id":1148466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1148214-chronicler-s-guide-and-other-1ed-books#post1148214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> Since the advent of the second edition, moast of the crunch (and some of the fluff) of the setting has been reworked, are there any plans to make second-edition-compliant versions of old books? Or a guide to update them?<br /> <br /> Specifically, I am looking for the ideas in the Chronicler's Guide ( I just love the concept of Soul Mods, getting a legacy attainment for practical reasons and getting drawbacks for doing so!) and how to update them to second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, waiting x years for a rehash of stuff already in print is not what i want OPP peeps to spend time and money on. I'd rather they focus on other stuff. Maybe a sidebar here and there pointing out a difference but whole new books? Nah, <br /> <br /> tldr, what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> said <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T16:43:51-07:00","id":1148469,"title":"","content":"As far as I know the next two books to come out that have been announced are Signs of Sorcery, then Tome of the Pentacle. I wouldn't be surprised if there was going to be a Player's Guide on the horizon, but I wouldn't expect it to show up anytime soon.<br /> <br /> You might look at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">the outline for Signs of Sorcery</a>, as while it's not like the old Chronicler's Guide it would tell you a lot of things to do as a Chronicler and how to do them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T16:49:46-07:00","id":1148470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1148214-chronicler-s-guide-and-other-1ed-books?p=1148469#post1148469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know the next two books to come out that have been announced are Signs of Sorcery, then Tome of the Pentacle. I wouldn't be surprised if there was going to be a Player's Guide on the horizon, but I wouldn't expect it to show up anytime soon.<br /> <br /> You might look at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/signs-of-sorcery-mage-the-awakening-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">the outline for Signs of Sorcery</a>, as while it's not like the old Chronicler's Guide it would tell you a lot of things to do as a Chronicler and how to do them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The third book was also mentioned, The Fallen World(s) or sommat, about mages and the other realms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T18:33:20-07:00","id":1148487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1148214-chronicler-s-guide-and-other-1ed-books?p=1148470#post1148470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third book was also mentioned, The Fallen World(s) or sommat, about mages and the other realms?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right.<br /> <br /> They're all mentioned <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}